# ---- HOST-NATIVE STATION (native from day one — fmtowns wave, 2026-09-13) ----
# Fujitsu FM TOWNS running Towns OS V2.1 L51 (TownsMENU) straight from the
# Towns System Software CD — no installed disk. MAME's fmtowns-family driver
# (src/mame/fujitsu/fmtowns.cpp, MACHINE_NOT_WORKING but boots Towns OS) runs
# ON THE HOST: drawshm frames, ctlsock keys through the generated keymap,
# sound -> FIFO with the daemon as clock. Launcher: shared
# stations/mame-native/x11-runtime.sh; reset = relaunch restoring the golden
# savestate (the driver registers its state: 109 save_item calls).
# The wave: docs/lab/FMTOWNS-WAVE.md.
SH_RESET_MODE=relaunch
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=Fujitsu FM TOWNS, Towns OS V2.1 L51 TownsMENU desktop booted from the Towns System Software CD (no installed disk), baked into the golden savestate so a visitor never sees the CD boot; details and measured numbers in docs/lab/FMTOWNS-WAVE.md.
MAME_NATIVE_BIN=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/fmtowns/mame-native/fmtowns
MAME_NATIVE_DRIVER=fmtownsftv
MAME_NATIVE_ROMS=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/fmtowns/mame-native/roms
MAME_NATIVE_GEOM=1024x768
# Every fmtowns-family machine is MACHINE_NOT_WORKING, so MAME raises its
# startup warning panel — which PAUSES a headless kiosk until a key is
# pressed. skip_warnings is only honoured with the skip-warnings patch
# (atari800xl's finding), which this station's binary carries.
MAME_NATIVE_SKIP_WARNINGS=1
# Golden stream, 2026-09-08: SAVEST at the menu (13 ms, 11871 bytes) restores
# via a fresh relaunch with -state golden pixel-identical to the baked frame
# (PIL diff bbox None) -- decision, not a default: keep =1.
MAME_NATIVE_CHECKPOINT=1
# Device set (fmtowns.cpp, 0.289): -pad1 townspad (the Towns 2-button pad),
# -pad2 mouse (the Towns mouse: an MSX-protocol mouse on the second pad
# port) — both driver defaults, set explicitly so a MAME default change can
# never silently drop one. -cdrom is the Towns System Software V2.1 L51 CD as
# a CHD composed by tiles/fmtowns.sh; the Towns boots from CD into
# TownsMENU with no disk installed. Two 3.5" HD floppies stay empty.
MAME_NATIVE_ARGS=-pad1 townspad -pad2 mouse -cdrom /data/vms/streamhost/assets/fmtowns/media/townsos-v21l51.chd
SH_MAMECTL_SOCK=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/fmtowns/ctl.sock
SH_MAMESOCK_KEYMAP=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/fmtowns/fmtowns.keymap
SH_AUDIO_SOURCE=fifo
SH_AUDIO_FIFO=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/fmtowns/audio.fifo

# ---- POINTER: proven 2026-09-13 (docs/lab/FMTOWNS-WAVE.md SS Pointer) ----
# The Towns mouse is an MSX general-purpose-port device (bus/msx/ctrl/
# mouse.cpp), tagged :pad2:mouse:BUTTONS/MOUSE_X/MOUSE_Y — NOT the SGI Indy's
# hle_ps2_mouse the fleet ctlsock module hardcodes, so mame-ctlsock-ptr-tags.patch
# (with its type-based Mouse-X/Y binding fix layered on top, native.d/fmtowns.sh)
# is required for the module to bind these fields at all. MEASURED on this
# binary: `ctlsock: setup btns=1 axes=1 movea=0 devxy=0 swap=0 sig=1ebe131a
# entries=3330` — sig/entries UNCHANGED from the pre-patch binary, so the
# existing golden .sta is not orphaned (rule 6).
MAME_CTL_PTR_TAGS=:pad2:mouse:BUTTONS,:pad2:mouse:MOUSE_X,:pad2:mouse:MOUSE_Y
MAME_CTL_BTN_NAMES=P2 Button 1,P2 Button 2,

# ---- ABSOLUTE POINTER, stated in Towns OS's own cursor word ----------------
# (mame-ctlsock-abs-ram.patch + mame-ctlsock-abs-ram-nudge.patch, applied last
# in native.d/fmtowns.sh). NO counts are issued for a MOVEA, which is the only
# way to be 1:1 here: the Towns OS mouse driver ACCELERATES, from 1.53 px per
# count at a 5-count poll to 5.83 at 40, with no linear region anywhere — so
# MAME_CTL_GAIN_X / MAME_CTL_GAIN_Y must NEVER be set on this station. No
# single value is right, and the open loop undershoots every target by the
# remainder chunk. docs/lab/FMTOWNS-WAVE.md SS Pointer streams #4 and #5.
#
# pts is ONE address on purpose. Towns OS mirrors the cursor into three word
# pairs; 0x0a2034 is a copy it rewrites every poll, and 0x116240 is the ERASE
# position — the rect the next poll restores before drawing. Write 0x116240
# and the old arrow is never removed, so the desktop fills with stale cursors
# (MEASURED on a clean LOADST golden; the table is in the wave doc). Writing
# 0x11623c alone propagates to all three AND erases correctly.
#
# nudge=1: Towns OS repaints only when a poll carries a non-zero delta, so the
# position is written pre-biased by one and one count is issued; the driver's
# own +1 (its curve is exactly 1.00 unit/count at n=1) lands on the commanded
# pixel and does the repaint.
#
# RECT is the letterbox measured from the frame (non-black bounds of the shm
# surface); GEOM is the Towns raster, derived from the px-per-guest-unit slope
# of the cursor word itself: 931 x 0.686 = 639 and 702 x 0.683 = 479, i.e.
# 640x480. PROVEN: five targets x two laps, the guest word EXACT on all ten.
MAME_CTL_ABS_RAM=cpu=maincpu,pts=0x11623c,order=hv,nudge=1
MAME_CTL_ABS_RECT=61,48,931,702
MAME_CTL_ABS_GEOM=640x480
# mame-ctlsock-btn-active-low.patch / MAME_CTL_BTN_ACTIVE_LOW is DELIBERATELY
# NOT here. MAME already applies the MSX BUTTONS port's IP_ACTIVE_LOW itself
# (ioport_port::read() XORs in the defvalue mask), so setting this env would
# invert an already-inverted polarity and turn every click into a no-op —
# measured with kh-fmtowns-padport-debug.patch (raw=f0->e0 on DOWN1, i.e. the
# guest sees button 1 pressed, with the env UNSET). See wave doc SS Pointer.
# The mouse is genuinely relative and truncates each poll's delta into a
# SIGNED BYTE (mouse.cpp), so a single MOVE must stay under 127 counts or it
# wraps; cap the daemon's rel-bridge chunk size well under that (measured
# ~6 px/count on both axes, positive sign).
SH_REL_MAX_STEP=100

SH_IDLE_PAUSE_SECS=60
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PIDFILE=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/fmtowns/mame.pid
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PROC_MATCH=assets/fmtowns/mame-native
MAME_NATIVE_STANDBY_DELAY_S=8

# Fleet floor for MAME keyboard stations (playbook §0): measure only if
# characters drop. A CPU-scanned matrix may need MAME_CTL_KEY_EXCL=1.
# 80/80, bbcmicro's values, not the 40/40 fleet floor: MEASURED from the real
# browser with the wire trace on (2026-09-08) — at 40/40 one demo line landed
# clean, at 80/80 three consecutive lines did, Enters and all.
SH_KEY_MIN_HOLD_MS=80
SH_KEY_MIN_GAP_MS=80
# EXCLUSIVE-SCAN (2026-09-08, operator's "the demo does not type"): the SAM's
# ROM scans the keyboard matrix itself and takes ONE key per scan, and the
# ctlsock module's hold/gap pacing is PER FIELD — so a burst of different keys
# (the SPA's type-in demo, a fast typist) lands several presses in the same
# frame and the ROM drops all but one: `10 MODE 4` arrived as `1  4`. With the
# port filter below a press on any kbd_N port waits until every other kbd_N
# field is up plus KEY_GAP (the mpf2/zxspectrum/dragon32 lesson); joy_0/1 are
# not matched. Proven with a raw 16-edge KEY burst through ctlsock: `PRINT 1`.
MAME_CTL_KEY_EXCL=:kbd_
